{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game","id":1364960,"title":"What's the plot of your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-03T00:49:21-08:00","id":1364960,"title":"What's the plot of your game?","content":"Are you breaking chains in the South? Uniting the tribes in the North? Manipulating nobles on the Isle? What's going on?<br /> <br /> My group is sailing the Western Ocean finding four ancient geomantic &quot;anchors&quot; that are binding a First Age Lunar Leviathan to the bottom of the sea, and they've heard nothing but contradictory stories of his motivations and why he was locked down there. They only have one anchor left before the big showdown- what does <b>Teeth of the Deep</b> want, and why was he imprisoned instead of killed?<br /> <br /> How about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T01:44:39-08:00","id":1364968,"title":"","content":"My 2 campaigns were :<br /> <br /> 1st campaign : Support your King to inherit the power of the Kingdoms next to Palanquin against his 2 big sisters, obviously this was totally inspired by The Princes of Amber (The former king name was Oron ...). Of course it complicated much more over the years with ancient prophecies, Abyssals that turns kingdoms against another, former Lunar Love that allies with the Abyssal because her Solar won't join her to go away in the Far North, fighting Wyld incursions in the Kingdoms, diplomating their way with the controlling-water-supply-isolationist-country, a 3rd Circle demon-imprisonned in a huge Obelisk their former selves created in their first incarnations, discovering they actually used the power of this demon to destroy many other enemies kingdoms during the First Age until their Zenith had a moment of clarity where they killed the whole Circle and imprisonned herself in the Obelisk to prevent anyone ever using that power again, convincing said Zenith they will find a way to destroy the Demon and lay her to rest after a watch of ten thousands year, the Night used the power of the demon during a limit break to destroy an enemy kingdom and curse it forever (ahahah I still can't get over this one it was awesome), the Twilight joined the new enemy Abyssal, that happened to be (hold yourselves) his son he had with his former mortal wife he lost his memory of when he decided to destroy his part of his soul he gave to his former Lunar Love so they could be reunited forever but that actually just drove her crazy over the millennia and he ended up killing her himself so she could be free of her ever maddening love, and so meanwhile his former mortal wife became crazy because she was the only one remembering her husband out of sheer love, and it drove their son insane as well so they ended up being merged into a soul-sharing Abyssal by the power of the 3rd Circle demon they didn't destroy when they had the opportunity, the Dawn killed the Eclipse during the big battle against the forces of the Abyssal while they had a very strong mentor-student bond but the Eclipse didn't control his power enough and out of a Limit Break we decided it was the most dramatic (after 2 years of campaign of really intense relationship between the 2) to have the Dawn kill him during the battle, where the Eclipse denied the repentance of the Dawn valorous enemy by killing him in the back when a peace option was being discussed.<br /> <br /> At the end of this campaign, I really understood why the Usurpation happened, because these Solars are damn crazy.<br /> <br /> It was my most intense campaign ever, that ended the worst for the characters that I ever STed ever, and it was FORKING AWESOME ! I never had so much drama, so much glorious wins and horrible loss for every characters, intensity in role-play, I even had 2 players thank me because it was their first time being so intensely pulled into their characters (honestly it was my first time feeling I did a good job as a ST), and I can never think that this is not thanks to the wonderful game that is Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'll post 2nd campaign later it was shorter but very fun as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 02-03-2020, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T03:41:11-08:00","id":1364981,"title":"","content":"So when I think about the game I would run, I always return to the same germ of an idea: The lovable waif who wasn't.<br /> <br /> Its a coming of age story where our circle comes into contact (hopefully as unobtrusively as I can manage as an ST) with said waif who idolizes them, wants to emulate their greatness. She/he/they become a constant companion, a side-kick of sorts, and the players see themselves meaningfully reflected in their gradual maturity.<br /> <br /> Of course multitudes of dark forces gather to either influence or kidnap said waif, but why?<br /> <br /> In my original telling (that I'm not saying has to be your telling) it's because the waif is a young primordial (and the first Creation born of their ilk) who represents the zeitgeist of the current age, and the players have a real opportunity to shape, but not stop, their apotheosis.<br /> <br /> I recall someone kindly made up a series of pseudo-charms to represent the growing power of the littlest primordial, I should go look for those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-03-2020, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T11:33:58-08:00","id":1365061,"title":"","content":"Right now I'm running a city building game.The players took over a low population/brink of destruction city (Only 1,000 living people, room for 10x that many.) Normally my players like to wander about so I thought it would be a nice change of pace to keep them in one area and make most of the threats being issues plaguing the people rather than direct combats. Strangely, no one wanted to play a social character despite being a city management campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T12:25:39-08:00","id":1365080,"title":"","content":"The game I'm running is based around Gem. The first sessions had plot, though they were mainly about establishing the city, familiarizing everyone with the districts and the society. The overall plot, though, revolves around one of the Sahlak daughters having been manipulated into falling head-over-heels in love with Makarios (the fact that he got statted for 3.0 was an unexpected bonus). Through various complicated manipulations involving a Fair Folk siege and a trio of powerful demon-bloods assisting her, she bought Makarios's hand in marriage for 100,000 marked souls and brought him into Creation, along with a city sculpted from dreams to supplant Gem. The Despot was driven from the city and is scheming to get his throne back and the characters are currently working to collect allies around the region to fight the Despotina and her consort. They also know that they need to figure out how to break a Malfean matrimonial contract so that Makarios will be expelled from Creation and thrown back into Hell. We're 67 games in now, so obviously there's been a bunch of other stuff that's happened, piles of various NPCs, and stories that have only somewhat interacted with the main plot. But long run, it's building up to the PCs finding a way to annul the marriage and probably to storm Gem with whatever forces they can muster and retake it. <br /> <br /> If and when they do that, they get to figure out what to do with the city. Run it and deal with the various hassles involved, leave it to some friendly king and go off in search of their past lives, or abandon it entirely and go off in search of other adventure. The PCs will probably have a lot of leeway at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T12:44:18-08:00","id":1365087,"title":"","content":"Currently I have a group that jumpstarted by accident a war between brightwork and onyx, and are currently handling the war effort while they stumble upon demonic conspiracies.<br /> <br /> And I'm playing a pair of monster of the week type of games with a monster hunter and a sword muse, both too fresh to have a visible overarching story..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T14:04:16-08:00","id":1365105,"title":"","content":"The PCs actually just discovered the plot (well, some of it) after... 13 sessions? Something like that. They're only Essence 2.<br /> <br /> The first story arc was the collapse of a Lunar-led kingdom due mostly to the corruption of the Changing Moon King and his court. But the collapse was incited and pushed by the Guild, a Raksha, and a group of mercenaries who wore blue-and-white, or red (I guess you could say vermillion), led by Dragonblood samurai and Yamabushi.<br /> <br /> In the second arc, while the Lunar PCs eventually made peace with the Dragonblood and got them to leave, the land was wracked by earthquakes and an eternal winter. If not ended, humanity may starve to death.<br /> When the PCs spied on the Dragonblood and talked to gods, they heard it rumoured that Mela's brothers Jormungandr the Earth Dragon, and Sutr the Fire Dragon, may be dead, and Mela might be angry, hence the winter. It seemed that the Sacred Land to the South, the Dragon Empire ruled by the Red Queen, has been destroyed by an army of demons; some call them the Nephilim (which translates as either &quot;giants&quot; or &quot;the fallen ones&quot;). Others call them the Yama Kings, the 666 <i>Kuromao</i>, the Black Devil Kings, the Prometheans.<br /> <br /> So the PCs went to investigate, by travelling to the Elemental Pole of Air. The No Moon believed the story about dragons dying was rubbish, and in fact Jormungandr had cast down Mela and was now in her palace attempting to destroy the world.<br /> <br /> When the Lunars reached Mela's castle (thanks to following a group of Dragonblood-piloted airships with wind-controlling Sail charms), they found demons fighting Dragonblood and their mortal ashigaru. They saved some Dragonblood and forced them to surrender and come with them. In Mela's ridiculously massive throne room, the Changing Moon met a group of strange people; they looked like normal humans from the North, but some carried strange weapons. They revealed their identity; an ancient, prehistoric form of Exalted. Long ago, they were not only Dragonblood and Lunars, but many other forms; Exigents, Getimians, Umbrals, Hearteaters, [something utterly unmemorable], and the Exalted of the Sun: the Solar Exalted. It is these &quot;Solar Exalted&quot; who have escaped Hell and returned to Creation. They haven't yet revealed their powers, but they seem to command demons, and several have implied that they're able to swap or steal bodies.<br /> <br /> The leader of the Solars, an old man named Te\u0161up, although he is better known by the name Yurgen Kaneko, Bull of the North, told the PCs that the Dragons long ago betrayed the Solars and cast them into Hell (hence presumably the term Nephilim, &quot;the Fallen Ones&quot;). Now, he claims, the Dragons plan an &quot;Impergium&quot;, an apocalypse that will destroy all of humanity. Thus, the Solars must kill the Dragons to save humanity.<br /> <br /> However, the Dragonblood captives claim that Mela is only unleashing Fimbulwinter to stop the Yama Kings. If the Demons are defeated, Mela will be safe and Fimbulwinter will end.<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon convinced the Solars to allow them to try negotiating with Mela first. Now, they walk across the massive icy cavern floor towards her massive throne, whose base is defended by an army.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, next session, maybe the PCs will make peace, maybe they'll fight prehistoric body-stealing sun-witches who spent 1500 years in Hell, or maybe they'll fight a bunch of Dragonblood and the Elemental Dragon of Air.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Mela will just freeze everyone to death. We'll see! I'm certainly pretty interested to see which way it goes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T14:10:03-08:00","id":1365107,"title":"","content":"First game: a group of exalts run around in the scavenger lands, being heroes, saving people, flying yeddim rockets, ramming wyld hunts with heavily armored yeddim rockets, sicking swarms of flesh-eating insects on wyld hunts<br /> <br /> Second game: a group of exalted murder-hobos muck around in the far north, looking for epic loot<br /> <br /> third game: a group of alchemical murder hobos much around in the south, usually inadvertently saving the day, maybe... also recycling dogs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T14:44:09-08:00","id":1365116,"title":"","content":"What's a plot?<br /> <br /> I tum up each week with popcorn and improvise. Which... uh... has kinda led to my character getting sent to hell and an unbound second circle demon being unleashed on Creation. I regret nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T15:03:39-08:00","id":1365123,"title":"","content":"The players were mortals on Crasari, a sea-turtle-esque behemoth five miles long and home to a small but thriving community of fishers and traders. At the start of things, an Abyssal arrived on the living island, bringing with him a strange jade arc, and proceeded to use a necromantic ritual to kill Crasari and throw her, and everyone on her back, deep into the Underworld. Unfortunately, he wasn't a very <i>good </i>Abyssal (and I still have no idea how to balance encounters), and the players killed him and took the arc. Since then, they've been trying to survive the bleak horror of death and get the thousand-some survivors back to Creation while not letting the Arc fall into the hands of any Deathlords.<br /> <br /> Along the way, the arc was opened and turned out to be carrying a bunch of Solar exaltations en route to being corrupted into Abyssal ones, the party ticked off Princess Magnificence With Lips of Coral (going by &quot;Black Heron&quot; and not currently a slave of FAFL in my version of things) and they met the Green Lady, a Mysterious Sidereal<sup>TM</sup> who hates Solars, keeps popping up, and seems to be playing all sides against the center.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 02-03-2020, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T17:07:27-08:00","id":1365141,"title":"","content":"Our game takes place in Vaneha. The holy mountain of Ama-Ni-Traya was taken over by a strange enemy leading an army of undead. One of the characters was a monk in the most important monastery on the mountain who exalted during his ritual seclusion in the sanctuary at the very top of the mountain only to discover that his fellow monks are slain.<br /> <br /> In order to find out what happen to them, together with the guardian spirit of the mountain, Taiyotora (apologies to all who actually speak Japanese), they tried to find Chinigo, the Wise Spirit of Izumi and discovered that he was sequestered and imprisoned in Yasal crystal by the clan Budzoke. With the help of other PCs, they managed to free Chinigo. They learned that under the Ama-Ni-Traya was located the tomb of their past incarnations and a powerful artifact called The Dam of Black River. Back in the First Age, they divided the spell allowing to control the Dam into three parts which they taught three Wise Spirits of Vaneha. The enemy was a powerful Abyssal, Face of the Void, who once used to be their circlemate.<br /> <br /> PCs managed to enter the tomb, a place of magitech wonder to discover chambers miles high containing millions of crystals. As they learned later, the Dam was built to trap the souls of dying and enable the rulers to &quot;manually&quot; control the reincarnation process in their kingdom. They retrieved crystals with the names of their own first-age predecessors, but had to leave the tomb, when the army of Face of the Void attacked and took over the manse. He also was looking for Three Wise Spirits to learn the spell controlling the Dam.<br /> <br /> Then they found the second Wise Spirit, Yorumi, and learned the second part of the spell convincing the spirit to reveal it, since he was worried of their pride which made them build the Dam in the first place. Meanwhile, they were uncovering a conspiracy in which some Vanehian aristocrats (with family connections to one of the PCs), factors of the Guild, an ambitious Realm officer were trying to provoke the war between Vaneha with the Realm which would be quickly ended with a treatise which will grant the Realm a strategically located part of Vaneha where Yellow River and Maruto river cross, and at the same time replace sword-prince Gensuji with one of the conspiracy members. The PCs were also fighting with a drug flooding Vaneha whose victims could apparently be controlled after death by conspiracy members. They learned that Face of Void is somehow involved in that plan.<br /> <br /> The protagonists decided to thwart the plan by turning one of the conspiring clans to their side. They reached it by bringing Furo Budzoke, nominally the head of the clan, back to the human form. Considered long dead, he was wandering for two hundred years in the shape of a crane because of the curse laid upon him. The clan Budzoke was each year purely ritually searching for him (as in. it was an actual rite they performed). Officially they had no leader, which was a source of a great disgrace for their clan. PCs wanted to perform a ritual which would bring him back to human form.<br /> <br /> However, one night before they finished preparations to the ritual, one of the crucial conspiracy members, the uncle of one of the PCs, Kehigo, contacted them and revealed that Face of Void knows where the third Wise Spirit is, but Kehigo can bring them to that very place before their enemy will reach it, using first-age portals which also played a prominent role before in the campaign (by the way, there is a Wyld zone in the space between those portals which they also visited). He offered them limited cooperation: they will not impede the plot to start the war and let them replace the ruling prince, but in turn they will be given an opportunity to stop the Abyssal from learning the third part of the spell (and, most likely, killing the third Wise Spirit of Vaneha).<br /> <br /> Facing the decision whether to stop the looming war with the Realm or to stop the Abyssal from reaching the Wise Spirit, they chose to stop the war. Currently two of three Wise Spirit are slain, Face of Void controls the Dam, Protagonists know two of three parts of the spell to control the Dam and so does their enemy. With this cliffhanger, we had to put the campaign on two-three months hiatus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-04-2020, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T17:23:35-08:00","id":1365146,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> After reading about your campaign I started asking myself whether my group actually plays Exalted. Tell us how it ended once you know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T01:54:29-08:00","id":1365194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365141#post1365141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the guardian spirit of the mountain, Taiyotora (apologies to all who actually speak Japanese).</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you Google'd &quot;Sun Tiger&quot;? that's a literal word swap. It's very close! Taiyo-no-Tora would be &quot;Tiger of the Sun&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T03:07:53-08:00","id":1365204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365194#post1365194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you Google'd &amp;quot;Sun Tiger&amp;quot;? that's a literal word swap. It's very close! Taiyo-no-Tora would be &amp;quot;Tiger of the Sun&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, actually when you translate from my mother tongue &quot;sun&quot; &quot;tiger&quot; and &quot;sun [genitive] tiger&quot; are different phrases and yield different translations, but the merged expression &quot;Taiyotora&quot; just sounds so much better that we sticked to it. It only feels stupid when you post it in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T03:42:17-08:00","id":1365210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365204#post1365204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, actually when you translate from my mother tongue &quot;sun&quot; &quot;tiger&quot; and &quot;sun [genitive] tiger&quot; are different phrases and yield different translations, but the merged expression &quot;Taiyotora&quot; just sounds so much better that we sticked to it. It only feels stupid when you post it in public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry because for the most of us that doesn't speak Japanese, it just sounds cool I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T07:39:23-08:00","id":1365252,"title":"","content":"Game 1 : Sandbox adventure set in the near east, it's been running for about 12 years now and not really likely to run out of material anytime soon.<br /> Game 2: Two Dynasts, a Ledaal and a Cathak on an expedition to find the lost city of Rathess.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T07:53:02-08:00","id":1365254,"title":"","content":"Te first game of ex3 I ran was in a kingdom near Vaneha and it didn\u2019t have much of an over arching plot aside from the characters personal growth. It had about 20 different locations of interest and each of them had their own mostly self contained stories.<br /> <br /> Second campaign took place a satrapy only the South. It was formerly comprised of two peoples, a culture that lived in the city with the aid of sorcery and Artiface, and a wide spread desert dwelling people that lived among the more fertile mountain areas and ranged into the dune sea. Then eventually the city people became infernally corrupted, began summoning demons and waging war on the desert people in an attempt to gather slaves and sacrifices without hurting their own citizens. Enter the Realm, who offered the desert people the deal of becoming a satrapy, marrying some Dynasts into their royalty to create a cadet house, and bending the knee to the Empire. In exchange they would help them take the city and all the treasures in it. The desert people agreed and with the support of Realm legions and Exalted overthrew the city. <br /> <br /> Centuries later the city is suffering. The water screws that once brought limitless fresh water up from underground are all but wrecked, the fountains no longer flow, the water spirits have become sickly, disease years through the impoverished parts of the city and in the background the smell of sulphur is in the air. The Realm is demanding more tribute while sending less aid to fix everything. A duo of Sidereals smell something is off so they manipulate a young group of solars into gathering together into the area, reckoning that unholy things don\u2019t last long in proximity to Solar exalted.<br /> <br /> From there the PCs worked from the shadows, staying hidden from the Dragonblooded while trying to fight a resurgence of demon worshipers in the satrapy, and somehow fix the water and disease problems. Eventually it was discovered that an Infernal exalt was using a sword to open gateways to hell and letting demons in, the twin of one of the PCs blades. On top of that House Cynis got fed up with this whole affair and sent a massive force to sort the problem out. Also the Wyld areas to the south had grumbling s of a Raksha lord wanting to take advantage of the whole situation. In the end the PCs managed to slay all the demons, make peace with the fry, and install themselves as the new leaders of the satrapy, totally unbeknownst to the Realm when the campaign ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:24:35-08:00","id":1365276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365146#post1365146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> After reading about your campaign I started asking myself whether my group actually plays Exalted. Tell us how it ended once you know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is probably quite important...<br /> <br /> I don't actually advocate that every game should lead to massive, world-shaking plot.<br /> <br /> My first 2e game ended with trying to stop Walker in Darkness spamming the Sword of Creation all over the world... but by that time I think one character was 700xp (and you got less xp back then). That's many years of sessions.<br /> <br /> In my 3e game, which was Essence 4-5, they... protected a jungle, took behind-the-thrones control of a few local kingdoms, and one character made her own small magic kingdom.<br /> That's it. From 200-350xp.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not every game needs to be balls-to-the-wall Elemental Dragons vs Incarnae.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the first story arc (which I skimmed over, as it's not the plot now, and was a kind of introduction), was just one small kingdom, the main villains were e2-3 Dragonblood and some weak Raksha, and a Guild merchant.<br /> <br /> The second arc was actually supposed to be the PCs fighting House Tepet's invasion of Iscomay. They kind of skipped that and went straight for the 3rd story arc (I don't mean each is a &quot;Story&quot; in the sense of wp and 1/story recovery).<br /> I didn't want to railroad them though, they seemed motivated to go to the Elemental Pole of Air and stop the Winter, so I just rolled with that. I was pretty excited to get to the Third Story Arc anyway, so I can get to the Fourth Story Arc. Which... actually is a lot less detailed than these ones, it's a bit sandboxy, I thought I could work out the details later, but we had more sessions than I expected, they're much more focused than I expected (normally these players bicker and piss around a lot, but they haven't in this game) so get through stuff faster, and of course they skipped from my planned Arc 1 to Arc 3 (which I'm fine with).<br /> Though perhaps after all this they'll return to the Kingdom they were in, and have to deal with House Tepet to the South anyway, before going on to the more sandboxy thing.<br /> <br /> But tbh, we've been playing Exalted for ages (13 years?) and I'm kind of bored. So I decided f*** it. Lunar PCs only, unlike the other 3 games full of Solars. Raksha because we've not really used them. Only Japanese-themed Dragonblood (so House Tepet), not Chinese-Roman. We'll put the game way, way in the North-East away from the normal stuff we've used a bunch. Nexus is a forest city because it's in the East. The Realm is destroyed. Pasiap and Hesiesh are dead. An Elemental Dragon who's destroying the entire world. The Realm say they're body-hopping spirits who possess people and stole power from the Unconquered Sun... so let's lean into that. (I'm not going to reveal exactly how accurate that is, but it's not entirely inaccurate in this game.)<br /> <br /> And let's throw in a bunch of Mesopotamian mythology (various Sumerian/Greek/Biblical flood myths and others). And some Indo-European stuff... all the Solars' true names are the names of Indo-European hero-gods who killed Dragons (Tarhunzas, Tesshub, Indra so far, the others will be similar).<br /> It fits Exalted yet actually isn't really used in the base game.<br /> Plus a bit of Asian stuff that again, is not really used in the base game but fits, hence the Yama Kings.<br /> <br /> The really interesting thing of course, is what happens if the PCs fail and Mela freezes the entire world...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-04-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:45:15-08:00","id":1365283,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad to see somebody using something from Creation itself as a world ending threat instead of Ishvara, Neverborn or Yozi. I find a lot of player sentiment to be that elementals and gods aren\u2019t really things that cause for much concern. Possibly because when they were first introduced to exalted they were sold on the idea that if a god is messing with you it\u2019s totally doable to go slap them around until they want to play nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:58:33-08:00","id":1365285,"title":"","content":"Thanks, though that wasn't intentional per-se.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I've used Abyssals loads, Infernals and the Ebon Dragon a bit, various random Dragonblood ,even Solars, as the main antagonists. So I thought what should I go for this time... and I decided on:<br /> One single Realm House (I chose Tepet as they're the most distinct from the others, in 3rd ed at least).<br /> Elementals and Gods, but purely Terrestrial ones.*<br /> Raksha<br /> (Each of these potentially could be allies or antagonists, depending on the PCs. 100% definitely the other side villains, like Yozis and the Neverborn, are dull to me.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, an angry goddess who's important to the world, but also threatening to destroy it, seemed appropriate to me. It fits with some of the Mesopotamian mythology that inspired my idea (I mean, you can't just deal with Zeus or Enlil or Yarwe flooding the world by killing them. Except this is Exalted so I guess you can, though it might not be a good idea!).<br /> <br /> *I don't generally enjoy plot about spirits. But I realised that actually what I don't like is plot about spirits who are far away in Yu-shan, or in sanctums, or dematerialised. Elementals are fine, because they can grab territory, can't dematerialise, etc. Terrestrial gods I got to work better than previously by thinking of them as, essentially, wacky community leaders/heroes rather than &quot;spirits&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:19:32-08:00","id":1365290,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve decided in the first arc of my new campaign that I\u2019m going to try and treat ghosts and spirits a bit differently. The last couple of campaigns I\u2019ve been in/run have either completely ignored them from existence, or treated them as very mundane and without any mystery. A house with a poltergeist was treated just like a rat infestation, hun souls as just kind of dull people. Even Ghostbusters treats ghosts with more mystery and its literally their job to bust ghosts!<br /> <br /> Gods and other spirits too, I\u2019m going to try to have more of a legendary or mythical vibe to them, and try to present them in a way that makes them feel like the amazing magical parts of nature turned up to impossible levels. Like a forest full of wood elementals should be like the Mirkwood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:52:43-08:00","id":1365301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365290#post1365290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve decided in the first arc of my new campaign that I\u2019m going to try and treat ghosts and spirits a bit differently. The last couple of campaigns I\u2019ve been in/run have either completely ignored them from existence, or treated them as very mundane and without any mystery. A house with a poltergeist was treated just like a rat infestation, hun souls as just kind of dull people. Even Ghostbusters treats ghosts with more mystery and its literally their job to bust ghosts!<br /> <br /> Gods and other spirits too, I\u2019m going to try to have more of a legendary or mythical vibe to them, and try to present them in a way that makes them feel like the amazing magical parts of nature turned up to impossible levels. Like a forest full of wood elementals should be like the Mirkwood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very interesting in hearing about your experience after your new test, because I have the exact same problem with my spirits and have no idea on how to handle them to make the &quot;poltergeist&quot; scene interesting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:37:12-08:00","id":1365309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365276#post1365276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this is probably quite important...<br /> <br /> I don't actually advocate that every game should lead to massive, world-shaking plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it wasn't meant to be very serious. I mostly just wanted to say that this campaign sounds cool (partly, I admit, due to the sheer scale).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:45:51-08:00","id":1365311,"title":"","content":"Yeah, me too.<br /> <br /> I always found it a bit irritating when gods and spirits seemed like... spies? Like they were always hanging out dematerialised, and then PCs would be like &quot;hmmm, what happened here... oh I'll just ask the god of this street&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> Ghosts as well to some extent.<br /> <br /> I think that with ghosts, maybe making them more mystical is the way to go, because it's too easy to just have them as... some guys.<br /> <br /> Whereas with gods, I found them<i> too</i> mystical, so they didn't really attach to the plot. I don't think making them just like humans is the way to go either... but I have found making them similar to Exalts, in a sense, works well. The god-plot I've found most interesting in my many years of gaming is probably the current plot in the game I play: Ahlat and friends are attempting to conquer the South and divide it up, like warlords.<br /> <br /> But just because it works for me, doesn't mean it works for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:47:20-08:00","id":1365313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365309#post1365309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, it wasn't meant to be very serious. I mostly just wanted to say that this campaign sounds cool (partly, I admit, due to the sheer scale).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am enjoying running it, more than my last campaign (I did generally enjoy that too, but there were bits I didn't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T13:19:05-08:00","id":1365338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365301#post1365301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm very interesting in hearing about your experience after your new test, because I have the exact same problem with my spirits and have no idea on how to handle them to make the &amp;quot;poltergeist&amp;quot; scene interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m on my phone right now so can\u2019t give a very detailed response, but a lot of it will have to do with how you describe things. First of all, you\u2019re the ST, break the rules a bit or make up your own. If you want to have the ghost of a drowned girl be able to flood any room of a house she\u2019s in with water and lock the doors, go for it. If you want a ghost appear just out of the corner of your eye, or have them create an illusion that the grand ballroom of their dilapidated castle has been restored to its full glory, it\u2019s done. Or more subtle creepy things, moving things that the players put down while they\u2019re not looking, have them instil sadness or rage while dematerialized, or have them boil eggs in their shells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365311#post1365311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas with gods, I found them<i> too</i> mystical, so they didn't really attach to the plot. I don't think making them just like humans is the way to go either... but I have found making them similar to Exalts, in a sense, works well. The god-plot I've found most interesting in my many years of gaming is probably the current plot in the game I play: Ahlat and friends are attempting to conquer the South and divide it up, like warlords.<br /> <br /> But just because it works for me, doesn't mean it works for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m leaning towards gods who are not interested so much in having direct control and concrete relationships with the mortal world, but still having a big effect on it most of the time. If they want to rule mortals they\u2019ll do it through worship and prophets rather than direct governance. When they show up personally it should be an event, and dealing with them a bit strange because they\u2019re beings who are from two worlds. Which isn\u2019t to say that they\u2019re absent, just that they\u2019re ageless beings who may have different methods and perspectives on things.<br /> <br /> I might liken them a bit to people who are like 40 year obsessive experts in their fields. Like I listened to an interview the other day with somebody who\u2019d studied caffeine and caffeinated drinks for the past decade and he was fairly convinced that the industrial revolution was initiated and made possible by caffeine. I don\u2019t really know if I agree with that but I can see a god of tea agreeing. The Queen of all Bees would probably tell you in great detail how much bees are needed to agriculture and all flowering plants, and how without bees no civilization would ever have been possible. Worship the bee, you owe it everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T16:44:05-08:00","id":1365394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365204#post1365204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, actually when you translate from my mother tongue &amp;quot;sun&amp;quot; &amp;quot;tiger&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;sun [genitive] tiger&amp;quot; are different phrases and yield different translations, but the merged expression &amp;quot;Taiyotora&amp;quot; just sounds so much better that we sticked to it. It only feels stupid when you post it in public.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im sorry. I didn't mean to make you feel bad about it. Japanese is a weird language and I get really excited helping people use it. <br /> <br /> What's your mother tongue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T17:32:42-08:00","id":1365405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365394#post1365394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im sorry. I didn't mean to make you feel bad about it. Japanese is a weird language and I get really excited helping people use it. </div> </div> </div> </div>I was rather worried about actual Japanese people on this forum, as merging words from a language you don't know until it sounds cool may be seen as mildly offensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365394#post1365394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your mother tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Polish. So yeah, I'm not at all inclined to think that you can juxtapose a couple of nouns and they will start functioning as adjectives. English is insanely flexible in this respect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, the character travelling with Taiyotora, upon the exaltation assumed a new name: Taiyoko. He is the wielder of an artifact wrackstaff, relic from the sanctuary, Taiyomono.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-04-2020, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T12:32:54-08:00","id":1365592,"title":"","content":"One of my favourite ways to handle spirits is a trick I got from a friend.<br /> Essentially that you humanise non-human NPCs appropriate to spiritual background of the person interacting with them. Especially for single splat games where Abyssal get to be unphased by most of the Underworld while the authority of a group of Sidereals forces most gods to talk to them on a similar level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T14:12:37-08:00","id":1365606,"title":"","content":"The plot of the current Exalted 3e game I'm running is that the Circle are a group of explorers from Autochthonia. The Tripartite Council of the Metropolis of Wisant, desperate to find some way out of the trap the Nation of Nurad found itself in, built Project Razor on their own initiative, without consulting the National Council, and sent the party through to recontact Creation. The members of the Circle all Exalted as Solars in the first few days after reaching Creation (the Zenith of the group, though, has since returned to Autochthonia full-time, and been replaced as a PC by an Alchemical). <br /> <br /> Since the breakthrough, the Circle has been exploring Creation (I'm doing a &quot;hexcrawl&quot;-style game, where each map area has an adventure hook or two, and needs to be surveyed to get a sense of what resources it contains). They're looking for sources of resources to help their city and Nation survive the oncoming disaster of being engulfed by the Blight. So far, they've discovered a couple of demesnes and manses, and made friends with some locals, some of whom have been inducted into the Nation of Nurad. They're currently travelling back to Autochthonia, where they've been summoned to address the National Tripartite Council of Nurad to provide a report on the Creation project, and probably to justify its continuation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:52:37-08:00","id":1370144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1364960-what-s-the-plot-of-your-game?p=1365146#post1365146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> After reading about your campaign I started asking myself whether my group actually plays Exalted. Tell us how it ended once you know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it hasn't ended per-se, but they went and negotiated with Mela. The shaman had heard the Solars conversing in a strange dialect of Old Realm, and warned the others that the Solars weren't interested in peace.<br /> The Changing Moon arranged a deal; the Lunars would help Mela fight the Solars... but only if she agreed to wrestle the Full Moon, Krove the Tiger-Bull. Didn't matter if she won or lost, he just wanted to wrestle a dragon.<br /> <br /> When she took her mighty Dragon form, the Solars attacked her, and the Lunars defended her. There was a huge battle, where Yurgen Kaneko revealed why he's known as the Bull of the North; he revealed his true form, a huge blue-skinned oni with bullhorns.<br /> <br /> There was a huge battle, which ended with almost everyone dead from either fighting each other, or Mela's brutal frost aura. The only two players still conscious grabbed their friends and the unconscious Yurgen Kaneko and fled.<br /> Anyhow, Mela is safe for now, the Solars are defeated. So hopefully now they can convince her to end Fimbulwinter.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure what they're going to do next (not sure they are either), but what I've got lined up for the next story arc is pretty shocking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-24-2020, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}